The agent that runs inside a target JVM contains no third-party code, except
that its optional hooks module carries a relocated copy of Byte Buddy
(Apache-2.0) and the ASM it bundles (BSD-3-Clause), whose notices travel inside
that jar under META-INF/third-party/; the module is loaded only when named.
The command line distribution redistributes a few third-party libraries
unmodified; they are listed, with their licences, in its THIRD-PARTY.txt.
Third-party libraries used by the controller, the sample application and the
build are listed, with their licences, in docs/licence-audit.md.
